<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Chemserve H1 shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Chemserve H1 shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		41.0	  vs 33.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 10.1	  vs 8.8</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   26.5	  vs 21.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   45.7	  vs 38.1</p>
<p>    Tax			 17.1	  vs 14.1</p>
<p>    Net finance costs     10.3	  vs 7.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		  595.0	 vs 487.0</p>
<p>Div payable September 1</p>
<p>on register August 15</p>
<p>Full name: Chemical Services Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that the outlook for the year was positive and the earnings and dividend forecasts for the full year remain at 98.0 and 27.5 cents per share respectively. Last year the firm posted earnings per share of 81.5 cents and a dividend of 23.7 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
